WEBVTT

00:00:00.285 --> 00:00:03.847
A service was ready in yesterday's replay,
and now it isn't.

00:00:04.018 --> 00:00:06.308
Start from its history to find the first

00:00:06.308 --> 00:00:08.884
replay that changed and what changed with
it.

00:00:09.452 --> 00:00:11.617
Open the service and switch to Readiness.

00:00:11.788 --> 00:00:12.971
Set the date range.

00:00:13.142 --> 00:00:15.885
Leave Build empty to see build changes, or

00:00:15.885 --> 00:00:19.476
select an image tag to compare runs of just
that build.

00:00:20.019 --> 00:00:23.275
Each column is a graded replay, oldest on
the left.

00:00:23.446 --> 00:00:26.481
Find the first Not ready column after a
Ready run.

00:00:26.652 --> 00:00:31.529
In this example, the latest replay drops
after two Ready runs of the same build.

00:00:32.085 --> 00:00:35.193
Read What moved in this range next to the
numbered marks.

00:00:35.364 --> 00:00:38.074
A mark may describe a new build, a changed

00:00:38.074 --> 00:00:41.172
grading rule, or a change in how the replay
ran.

00:00:41.343 --> 00:00:43.851
Use the labels to see what applied to this
run.

00:00:44.419 --> 00:00:48.070
Use Behind the letters to compare the
actual measure to its floor.

00:00:48.241 --> 00:00:50.361
Here, the regression pass rate dipped.

00:00:50.532 --> 00:00:53.064
Open the replay column for the Readiness

00:00:53.064 --> 00:00:56.545
tab, or select the family letter to jump to
its detail.

00:00:57.085 --> 00:01:00.994
Start your investigation with the report
where the verdict first changed.
